  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "My heart, really. It's been fluttering, like it skips and then races, mostly in the evenings when I finally sit down.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:26",
      "end_timestamp": "00:37",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Well, like I said, it flutters. Sometimes it's a few seconds, sometimes it goes on for a minute or so, and it happens a few evenings a week.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:44",
      "end_timestamp": "00:59",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I see. And when did you first notice it?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:26",
      "end_timestamp": "01:32",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Ooh. Um. It could have been last month, or the month before that, I honestly couldn't tell you. It sort of crept up on me.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:33",
      "end_timestamp": "01:46",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That's perfectly all right. I can see in your notes that you take carbimazole. What dose are you on at the moment?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:55",
      "end_timestamp": "02:05",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Twenty... maybe 20 mg? It was changed at some point, I think, or I think it was. The box is in my other bag, sorry.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:08",
      "end_timestamp": "02:23",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Don't apologise. How often do you take it?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:24",
      "end_timestamp": "02:29",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Once a day, in the morning with breakfast. That's the one thing I never forget, because the alarm on my phone goes off.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:31",
      "end_timestamp": "02:42",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I hear you. Before I decide anything, are you allergic to any medicines, now or in the past?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:06",
      "end_timestamp": "04:15",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Penicillin. I came out in hives when I was about six, my mum always reminds me, and I've avoided it ever since.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:18",
      "end_timestamp": "04:30",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Please don't give up the tablets. I'd rather you called me first. What I think is most likely is the thyroid hormone level not being fully settled yet.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:53",
      "end_timestamp": "06:06",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's my best working guess, based on what you've told me. I'd like to repeat your thyroid blood test today so we aren't relying on guesswork.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:17",
      "end_timestamp": "06:29",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Keep taking the carbimazole exactly the way you have been. And if the fluttering ever comes with a racing heart that won't settle, faintness or chest pain, ring 999 rather than waiting for us.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:12",
      "end_timestamp": "07:28",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's actually quite important with that medicine. A sore throat with a fever should be checked quickly, so do mention it if it ever happens.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:43",
      "end_timestamp": "07:57",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    }
